  render_p(sec33, "The spectral gap of the Cayley graph Cayley(Z/N, +-e_i) is gap = 4*sin^2(pi/q_max) where q_max is the largest prime-power channel width. In the 108 lambda-420 heartbeat lattice, b^2=49 is forced (TWO-CONSTRAINT theorem) and strictly dominates D^4=16, K^2=9, E^2=25, L=11, GATE=13. Therefore q_max=49 uniformly. The gap is constant across the entire 108-ring lattice — a structural analog of the Yang-Mills mass gap, restricted to abelian Cayley graphs on the heartbeat fiber.");
